course: dictionary
lesson: 12742
title: Drugged: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change a little depending on the sentence around them. Drugged is one of them. The clues are in the other words: «The guard's drink tasted odd, and soon he felt drugged and could not keep his eyes open.» Felt drugged means sleepy, slow and confused, so the word describes how a person feels.
explain: Drugged can also describe a drink or food. «She found a drugged drink on the table and told an adult straight away.» Here drugged means something has been secretly put into the drink. Ask yourself: is the word describing a person or a thing? The clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Drugged is the past form of the verb drug. «Someone drugged the guard so the thief could sneak past.» Here drug means to give someone a drug secretly, against their will. Check by swapping in your meaning: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Drugged is the past form of the verb drug: drug, drugs, drugged, drugging.
fact: «Drugged» can describe a person who feels sleepy, slow or confused because of medicine.
fact: «Drugged» can describe food or drink that has a drug secretly put in it. Never accept drinks from strangers, and tell an adult straight away if you are worried.
fact: At the vet, animals may be drugged to keep them calm.
fact: In every meaning, something has been given a drug that changes how a person or animal feels or acts.
exercise: «Ravi felt drugged after his medicine and could barely keep his eyes open.» What does drugged mean here? | Loud and busy | Wet from the rain | *Sleepy and slow from medicine | Very happy and full of energy
exercise: «Ella's teacher said: never accept a drink from a stranger, and tell an adult if someone acts drugged.» What should you do? | Give it to your friend to try | *Tell an adult straight away | Drink it quickly before anyone sees | Keep it and hide it in your bag
exercise: The vet said the dog would be drugged to keep it calm. What does drugged mean? | Running fast across the field | Covered in mud | *Given a drug to keep it calm | Very hungry
test: «The villain drugged the guard's drink, and the guard fell asleep at his post.» What did the villain do? | Told the guard a joke | *Secretly put a drug in the guard's drink | Washed the cup | Gave the guard a present
test: «Lily felt drugged and confused after the medicine, so she lay down to rest.» What does drugged mean? | Wet and cold | Full of energy | *Sleepy, slow and confused from medicine | Hungry for lunch
exam: Which word means a drink has had a drug secretly put in it? | Curt | Luminous | *Drugged | Barely
